@@ -174,6 +174,8 @@ E-Hentai verification, browsing, favorites, and remote settings use one Hayai ne
 
 ## Novel reading stability
 
+The October reader batch guards WebView result delivery by document and focus generation, keeps speech callbacks on the main thread, distinguishes an explicit speech seek from a document refresh, and reuses content sheets for language, downloaded-entry search, and word statistics. Manual Novel selection uses J2K's custom genre data rather than a second type column. Image-preview handoff for such entries opens the selected chapter without applying an image-page index; image-only sources report their missing text capability instead of crashing navigation. Removing the manual tag does not negate a live novel source marker or existing durable novel evidence. Shared HTML normalization excludes head metadata and removes only an exact matching leading chapter heading, leaving the renderer responsible for its single optional title; explicitly enabled EPUB head styles and scripts retain their existing gates. Continuous Web chapter detection samples the reading area below the configured top inset, so seeking into a short final chapter reports that chapter instead of its predecessor at 100 percent.
+
 Reader quotes, highlight browsing/editing, chapter statistics, selected-text translation results, and imported fonts share a Hayai content-sheet assembly built from J2K's `E2EBottomSheetDialog`, Material toolbar/buttons/text fields, the existing `MaterialSpinnerView`, and Android's two-line RecyclerView rows. It reuses the existing rounded sheet surface, adds no J2K adapter, and leaves destructive confirmations as dialogs. Quote bodies remain selectable; save controls stay outside scrolling forms, and the sheet expands above an open keyboard using system insets. Legacy quote JSON recovery is retained only in the saved-quotes overflow menu. Storage, ordering, migration, and backup formats are unchanged.
 
 The September 2026 reader corrections reference Tsundoku commit `fe54f05ae038cbc2ae72713c6ac68a2fbccb11af`, especially `textview/NovelViewer.kt` and its chapter containment, selectable text, and viewport preservation behavior. The Hayai viewer keeps existing chapter blocks across preload notifications. It inserts or removes adjacent blocks without replacing the visible document. J2K receives the selected chapter's `NovelProgressPage` through `onPageSelected`; scrolling across a boundary no longer invokes the menu-oriented chapter loader, which can restore a different saved position.
